Commands for managing the Kubernetes cluster

Usage:
  mcp-runtime cluster [command]

Available Commands:
  cert               Manage cert-manager resources
  config             Configure cluster settings
  diagnostics        Diagnose an installed MCP Runtime cluster
  doctor             Check whether a cluster is ready for MCP Runtime setup
  identity           Inspect workload adapter identity health
  init               Initialize cluster configuration
  mcp-auth-connector Manage the bundled MCP Auth identity connector
  mcp-auth-gateway   Install the optional credential gateway and wire MCP Auth to it
  operator-rbac      Reconcile operator permissions from this release
  provision          Provision a new cluster
  status             Check cluster status

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for cluster

Global Flags:
      --debug   Enable debug mode with structured error logging

Use "mcp-runtime cluster [command] --help" for more information about a command.
